      <h2>Glossary: terms used in this guide</h2>

      <dl class="not-prose grid gap-3 text-sm">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">FSM (Field Service Management)</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Umbrella category for software that manages dispatching, scheduling, invoicing, and customer communication for businesses with technicians in the field. Used interchangeably with "field service software."</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Dispatching</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">The process of assigning jobs to specific technicians based on skill, location, and availability. Some dispatch tools also suggest routes or match technician skills to jobs; check each review's feature list.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Service agreement</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">A recurring contract where customers pay annually or monthly for scheduled maintenance + priority service. Common in HVAC and commercial plumbing.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Pricebook</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">A standardized catalog of services and prices used to generate quotes consistently across techs. Some platforms package it as a named feature, such as ServiceTitan's Pricebook Pro.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Flat-rate pricing</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Quoting the same price for the same job regardless of how long it takes, using set prices such as those in a pricebook. Opposite of time-and-materials billing.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">AIA billing</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">An invoicing standard used in commercial construction and large contracting projects. Progress billing on standard AIA payment-application forms, which bill the share of work completed against a schedule of values. If your customers require it, check that your software supports it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Two-way QuickBooks sync</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Bidirectional data flow between FSM software and QuickBooks. Changes in either system propagate to the other. Critical if your accountant makes adjustments directly in QB.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Consumer financing</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Financing offers (such as Wisetack, GreenSky or Synchrony) that let customers pay for large repairs over time. Some field service platforms connect a lender to estimates and invoices: <a href="https://www.wisetack.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" class="underline hover:text-slate-900">Wisetack's site lists</a> Housecall Pro and Jobber among its partners.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">GLS (Google Local Services Ads)</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Google's "Local Services" ad placement (with the green check).{glsTools.length > 0 && (<> Of the tools on this page, {glsTools.map((t, i) => (<>{i > 0 ? (i === glsTools.length - 1 ? ' and ' : ', ') : ''}<a href={`/tools/${t.slug}/`} class="underline hover:text-slate-900">{t.name}</a></>))}{' '}{glsTools.length === 1 ? 'lists' : 'list'} a Google Local Services integration.</>)}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
